Bugfix: Make the file list header keyboard operable and name its controls

The three sortable column headers of the file list were anchors without an href.
Such an anchor is not part of the tab order, so sorting by name, size or
modification date could not be reached with a keyboard at all, even though the
headers were fully operable with a mouse. They are now buttons, which are
focusable without a tabindex and respond to both Enter and Space.

The hidden file input that opens the upload dialog had no accessible name. Its
label is created lazily by the "New" menu, so a keyboard user tabbing through the
page - who cannot operate that menu, because its upload entry is a label - always
met an unnamed control. It now carries an aria-label using the same string as the
menu entry.

The two icon-only controls of the selection bar, which are the only download and
delete controls below 768px, received visually hidden text.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 2.1.1, SC 3.3.2, SC 4.1.2
